 "text": "Hey there, how are you? I like ten minutes per finger width of thickest layer, so ten minutes or so for thin oil painting. Rough sand between coats with an abrasive grit. You still have time to give it a light dust with a dusting brush, or even leave it as a surprise and only check just before presenting. You can spray it with a few coats of clear spray varnish, then dust it the day after. Spray on the box first, then on any tools that come with it. It feel firm to the touch, and the drying room won't make your nose glow either.",
